spec:
  grid: 16-19 rows x 16-19 cols; only colors 0 (black bg) and 1 (blue fg) in input; output adds 7 (orange)
  layout:
    description: |
      Grid is tiled/partitioned into 2-5 large, near-rectangular regions that alternate blue (1) vs black (0).
      Typical patterns: horizontal stripes, one-big-region + inset-rectangle, or L-shaped split.
    large_blue_regions: 1-3 regions, each >= ~30 cells, fill fraction >= 0.5 of its bbox
    large_black_regions: 1-3 regions, each >= ~40 cells (plus one may be as small as ~4 with leaves)
  defects (inside blue regions, become orange-haloed in output):
    count: 2-9 per grid
    shape: connected black components of size 1-3 (1-cell most common, occasional 2-3)
    placement: strictly inside a blue region (every 4-neighbor is blue or grid-border)
  leaves (dangling tips of large-black regions that protrude into blue, also haloed):
    count: 0-4 per grid; can be 0
    definition: pixel of a large (>3) black component with <=1 black 4-neighbor within the component
  spurs (small blue specks inside black regions, ABSORBED / not marked):
    count: 2-6 per grid
    shape: single blue pixel (occasionally 2) surrounded by black on >=3 of its 4-neighbors (corners count out-of-bounds)
    placement: inside a large black region interior
  output_rule: |
    For each defect-pixel-set and each leaf pixel, paint color 7 (orange) in the 3x3 Chebyshev
    neighborhood, EXCEPT the defect/leaf pixel itself stays 0 (black). Halos may overlap and may
    extend across blue/black region boundary (overwriting either color). Spurs are converted to 0.
  example_ascii: |
